  "description": "T1. Hornbeam Tree\t\r\n\r\nRear Garden:\r\n\r\nReduce new growth to previous reduction points (1.5m), retaining good growth furnishings to support crown development.\r\nIf required, thin the branch structure to help create an even balance.\r\nRemove dead branches over 2.5cm in diameter.\r\nInspect the crown for adversities and advise if necessary.\r\n\r\nThe tree's current height is 14m, and its crown spread is 8m\r\nAfter the proposed works, the tree's height is 12.5m and the crown spread is 6.5m \r\n\r\n\r\nT2. Chanticleer Pear\t\r\n\r\nFront/Side Garden:\r\n\r\nReduce new growth to previous reduction points (1.5m), retaining good growth furnishings to support crown development.\r\nIf required, thin the branch structure to help create an even balance.\r\nRemove dead branches over 2.5cm in diameter.\r\nInspect the crown for adversities and advise if necessary.\r\n\r\nThe tree's current height is 14m, and its crown spread is 8m\r\nAfter the proposed works, the tree's height is 12.5m and the crown spread is 6.5m  \r\n\r\n\r\nT3. Whitebeam\t\r\n\r\nRear Garden:\r\n\r\nSelectively reduce the height and spread by 1.5m, pruning out the longer sections of the stems, and leaving natural secondary branches to create a rounded appearance. \r\n\r\nThe tree's current height is 5m, and its crown spread is 3m\r\nAfter the proposed works, the tree's height is 3.5m and the crown spread is 1.5m",
